@startuml Storage_Area_Management_SSD
title Sequence Diagram – US 2.2.4 “Register and update storage areas, so that (un)loading and storage operations can be assigned to the correct locations.”

actor "Logistics Operator" as Operator
boundary "StorageAreaController\n(API Layer)" as Controller
control "StorageAreaService\n(Application Layer)" as Service
entity "StorageAreaRepository\n(Persistence Layer)" as Repo
entity "StorageArea / Warehouse / ContainerYard\n(Domain Layer)" as Domain
database "PortManagementContext\n(Infrastructure Layer)" as DB

' ===========================
' CONTEXT
' ===========================
note over Operator
User Story 2.2.4 – Register and Manage Storage Areas

"As a Port Authority Officer, I want to register and update
 storage areas, so that (un)loading and storage operations
  can be assigned to the correct locations."
end note

== CREATE STORAGE AREA (Warehouse or Container Yard) ==

Operator -> Controller: POST /api/storageareas\n(StorageAreaDTO)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: RegisterStorageAreaAsync(dto)
activate Service

Service -> Domain: new Warehouse(...) or new ContainerYard(...)
activate Domain
Domain --> Service: Validated Domain Entity
deactivate Domain

note over Service
Business Rules:
- Name cannot be empty
- MaxCapacity ≥ CurrentOccupancy
- SpecializedCargoType required for Warehouse
- For ContainerYard: may include YardType (e.g., Reefer, Dry)
end note

Service -> Repo: AddAsync(StorageArea)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: INSERT INTO StorageAreas (...)
activate DB
DB --> Repo: OK
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: StorageArea persisted
deactivate Repo

Service --> Controller: Created StorageAreaDTO
deactivate Service

Controller --> Operator: 201 Created + StorageAreaDTO
deactivate Controller


== UPDATE STORAGE AREA ==

Operator -> Controller: PUT /api/storageareas/{id}\n(StorageAreaDTO)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: UpdateStorageAreaAsync(id, dto)
activate Service

Service -> Repo: GetByIdAsync(id)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM StorageAreas WHERE Id = {id}
DB --> Repo: Existing StorageArea
Repo --> Service: Existing StorageArea
deactivate Repo

alt StorageArea Found
    Service -> Domain: Update properties (e.g., MaxCapacity, Occupancy, CargoType)
    activate Domain
    Domain --> Service: Updated Entity
    deactivate Domain

    Service -> Repo: UpdateAsync(StorageArea)
    activate Repo
    Repo -> DB: UPDATE StorageAreas SET ...
    DB --> Repo: OK
    Repo --> Service: Updated
    deactivate Repo

    Service --> Controller: NoContent
    Controller --> Operator: 204 No Content
else Not Found
    Service --> Controller: null
    Controller --> Operator: 404 Not Found
end
deactivate Service
deactivate Controller


== LINK STORAGE AREA TO DOCK ==

Operator -> Controller: POST /api/storageareas/{id}/link-dock\n(DockConnectionDTO)
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: LinkToDockAsync(storageAreaId, dockId, distance, travelTime)
activate Service

Service -> Repo: GetByIdAsync(storageAreaId)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM StorageAreas WHERE Id = storageAreaId
DB --> Repo: StorageArea
Repo --> Service: StorageArea
deactivate Repo

Service -> Domain: AddDockConnection(new DockStorageAreaConnection(...))
activate Domain
Domain --> Service: Connection added
deactivate Domain

Service -> Repo: UpdateAsync(StorageArea)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: UPDATE StorageAreas SET DockConnections=...
DB --> Repo: OK
Repo --> Service: Updated
deactivate Repo

Service --> Controller: 200 OK + Updated StorageAreaDTO
Controller --> Operator: Storage Area linked to Dock successfully
deactivate Service
deactivate Controller


== REMOVE STORAGE AREA ==
Operator -> Controller: DELETE /api/storageareas/{id}
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: DeleteAsync(id)
activate Service
Service -> Repo: DeleteAsync(id)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: DELETE FROM StorageAreas WHERE Id = {id}
DB --> Repo: OK
Repo --> Service: Deleted
deactivate Repo
Service --> Controller: NoContent
Controller --> Operator: 204 No Content (Storage Area removed)
deactivate Service
deactivate Controller

@enduml
